# Port patch (0.99.17, the owner's decision of 17.11.2026 -- his standing rule: a game restriction gets
# fixed in the decompiled code rather than worked around; "let's go with the open planner thing"). Applied
# after patch 0231 (it extends that patch's hook in EmSetFromList).
#
# A room whose enemy list the game itself never fills -- the farm at the game's start (r120) has scenery
# only, its list slice is empty -- could never randomize: EmSetFromList skips every entry whose be_flag
# bit 0 is clear, and the room owns no entries at all. The randomizer now switches on a few of the room's
# empty entries before the loop runs (re4_enemy_random_seed_list, runtime/enemy_random.cpp): a seeded
# entry gets the aliveness bit the loop needs, the "set" toggle bit the room's own code reads, an enemy id
# and a place the randomizer picked from the room's scenery, so the room plans and populates like any other.
# The list is the room's own copy in memory, never written into a save; the room's script keeps its cast,
# its named and area-waited entries untouched, and the seeding refuses rooms outside the story's Leon part,
# the extra games and boss rooms.
--- a/src/game/em_set.cpp
